For every $n\ge0$, $$\label{word:catalan-equation}
 a_nu^n\le \frac{1}{4^n(n+1)}\binom{2n}{n}
          =O\bigl((n+1)^{-3/2}\bigr).$$

Every nontrivial rooted planar map is uniquely obtained from a rooted block by inserting a rooted map, possibly trivial, in each of its corners. A nonempty insert is attached at the origin of its root dart. Moreover, $a$ is multiplicative when two maps are joined at one vertex. Consequently, with $$T(z)=\sum_{n\ge0}a_nz^n,\qquad
 \Phi(y)=1+\sum_{m\ge1}b_my^m,$$ there is an identity of formal power series $$\label{block:equation}
 T(z)=\Phi\big(zT(z)^2\big).$$

Suppose $T$ and $\Phi$ have nonnegative coefficients and constant term $1$, and satisfy <a href="#block:equation" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="block:equation">[block:equation]</a>. Let $u>0$ satisfy $T(u)<\infty$, and suppose that, for some $c>0$, $$\label{block:lower-assumption}
 \sum_{n\ge1}na_nu^nx^n\ge c(1-x)^{-1/2}
 \qquad\text{for all $x<1$ sufficiently close to $1$}.$$ Put $\tau=T(u)$ and $v=u\tau^2$. Then $$\label{block:critical-equations}
 \Phi(v)=\tau,\qquad
 2v\Phi'(v)=\Phi(v),\qquad
 \Phi''(v)<\infty,$$ where endpoint derivatives denote the corresponding nonnegative series.

Under <a href="#tree:assumptions" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="tree:assumptions">[tree:assumptions]</a>, $$\left(\frac{W_{Nt}}{\sigma\sqrt N},
       \frac{\sigma H_{Nt}}{2\sqrt N}\right)_{0\leq t\leq1}
 \ \Longrightarrow\ (e(t),e(t))_{0\leq t\leq1}
 \quad\hbox{in }C([0,1],\mathbb R^2),
 \label{tree:walk-limit}$$ where $e$ is a standard normalized Brownian excursion.
